# V23.9.14 — SMOOTH CORE / SINGLE SCHEDULER / BOUNDED FLOW
# =============================================================================
# PERFORMANCE-ONLY architecture pass. The V23.9.13 rolling-consensus lock logic,
# V23.9.11 loss memory, V23.9.10 strike lock, Original Tug authority, Zoro UI,
# grading, and end-path mapping remain authoritative.
#
# Why V23.9.13 could still feel laggy:
#   * years of layered UI revisions left multiple independent Tk `after()` trees
#     alive at the same time (dashboard, telemetry, MBI, grading, target guard,
#     lock heartbeat, journal, audit, watchdog).
#   * repeated StringVar.set() calls repainted unchanged labels.
#   * dashboard flow still scanned raw executions even though only 60 seconds of
#     flow are needed.
#   * Original Tug / native flow could be recomputed several times inside the
#     same ~100-200 ms UI slice by different consumers.
